0 FILE hogwarts-castle-v0.ldr
0 !BRICK_STATE {"schema_version":3,"status":"instruction_reconstruction_in_progress","version_label":"버전 0","reference_set":"LEGO Harry Potter Hogwarts Castle (71043)","source_manual_segments":["6590084-80.pdf","6590084-145.pdf","6607899-54.pdf","6607899-95.pdf","6607899-150.pdf","6607899-194.pdf","6607900-70.pdf","6607900-125.pdf","6607900-165.pdf","6607900-182.pdf","6607901-50.pdf","6607901-106.pdf","6607904.pdf (official current booklet 3, inspected PDF pp.10–11)"],"coverage":"Official current 71043 booklet 3 (6607904.pdf), PDF pp.10–11 / printed pp.10–11, steps1–5 inspected directly as images and cross-checked against instruction_sets[\"71043\"] and registered DAT candidates. The root step1–7 block references are corrected to 3702 (yellow 1x8), 3703 (dark bluish gray 1x16), 32531 (light bluish gray studded 4x6 frame), four 6232, and one 2458. Exact connector-to-hole contacts and downstream step5–7 transforms remain provisional. Official booklet 3 PDF p.12 steps6–7 were also image-reviewed: step6 shows a long studless beam (32278 is a shape candidate but not present in the extracted 71043 inventory candidates), a gray wedge-like plate, a long gray plate, and a white plate; step7 shows three gray 2x2 bricks, one gray slope, one dark-green slope, and two olive-green slopes. No absent gray 3003 inventory entry or mismatched plate candidate is being treated as confirmed. The user-uploaded 6607901-50.pdf is a separate booklet 22 segment (printed pp.10–18); its step numbers are not combined with booklet 3.","piece_count":25,"placement_status":"Official booklet 3 p.10–11 candidate identity corrections are applied in hogwarts-frame.ldr: part-0001=3702; part-0006=3703; part-00030=32531; part-0007 and part-0009–0011=6232; part-0008=2458. This replaces the former 32524/32278/64179 and five 3700 candidate identities. The four step1 2780 references remain pending exact joint reassessment against the corrected 3702/32531 geometry. Candidate connector positions are explicitly provisional and are not considered verified merely because instance IDs resolve. Later booklet 22 modules/steps remain separately recorded; no GoBricks SKU is asserted. Official booklet 3 p.12 parts are being re-identified against the set inventory: the existing 32278 long-beam candidate is absent from extracted inventory; p.12 step7 2x2 gray-brick callout is not accepted as 3003 because the inventory has no gray 3003 entry. Existing p.12 references are provisional pending exact inventory candidate and stud-position matching.","validation":{"part_files":"shared LDraw shapes referenced","physical_fit":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.10–11 part silhouettes and callout counts are matched to registered 3702, 3703, 32531, 6232 and 2458 assets and the set inventory. Physical multi-contact fit is not yet verified for corrected root frame. Prior fit claims involving 32524, 32278, 64179, or 3700 in this root segment are superseded. Other separate local modules retain their previously recorded limited geometric checks.","full_manual_coverage":"in_progress","geometry_checks":"instance IDs, transforms, quantities checked locally; full validator requires catalog offer metadata not verified"},"steps":[{"pages":"10–12 (official booklet 3 PDF pp.10–12); steps5–7 candidate identities/positions remain provisional","steps":[1,7],"evidence":"Current official 71043 booklet 3 (6607904.pdf) p.10 steps1–2 and p.11 steps3–5 inspected directly as images. p.10 identifies 3702, 3703 and 32531 by studded shape and hole pattern; p.11 callouts identify one 6232 plus one 2458 at step3, then three more 6232 at step4. Existing later step5–7 coordinates require downstream re-registration. PDF p.12 steps6–7 were inspected as images. Step6 shows a long studless beam, gray wedge-like plate, long gray plate and white plate; 32278 matches the beam silhouette but is absent from extracted set inventory. Step7 callout counts three gray 2x2 bricks, one gray slope, one dark-green slope and two olive-green slopes; available inventory colors do not uniquely confirm the existing root candidates.","placement":"Corrected types and inventory-backed colors are stored in root hogwarts-frame.ldr with one ID/state record per physical part. Root connector positions are provisional; attachment to the 32531 frame and subsequent step5–7 geometry require contact-based refinement. The older step5–7 references remain candidates only; no identity or contact is inferred from their current positions."},{"pages":"13","steps":[8],"evidence":"Printed p.13 step8 parts and sequence: 64179 open-center 5x7 frame, 32278 long Technic rail, two 2780 pins, two purple 2420 corner plates, one lime 2x2 axle-hole plate, one gray 1x2 connector and two gray 2x2 side-pin connectors. Step1 inserts pins into the rail; step2 joins the frame; step3 turns the ring subassembly.","placement":"Local hogwarts-step8.ldr has frame 64179, two opposite-corner 2420 plates, 32278 rail, two 2780 pins, two 30000 end blocks, centered lime 4032a plate and gray 3700 brick candidate. Frame/rail axes at z=±60 are collinear with 10-LDU separation along X; two pins cross the seam. The built-in 30000 pins at z=±140 align with rail outer-face holes and insert ~18.5/20 LDU. 4032a studs meet the 3700 candidate base at y=-10, but the shown side projection remains unresolved. Partial and not root reachable."},{"pages":"17–18","steps":[14,15,16],"evidence":"Printed p.17 step14 makes a yellow 32524 beam with four 2780 pins; step15 adds a 64179 frame and 32278 long rail. Printed p.18 step16 calls out four pins and two gray 30000 blocks; the four pins enter the unused 32278 rail holes, and the red arrow identifies one 30000 pin entering an outer 64179 frame hole; the second block is shown at the long-rail end.","placement":"Local hogwarts-step14.ldr contains the 32524/four-pin beam, 64179 frame, and 32278 rail. The step17 64179/four-pin frame is now nested with a calculated transform and all four pins mate to the rail row. The combined step14–17 module is still not root-reachable; its global tie to steps1–13 is unresolved. Step16 pins use rail local holes z=20,60,100,140; pin +X axes are rotated to rail +Y and their origins sit at y=10 for an 18-LDU nominal insertion into its 20-LDU thickness. One 30000 is placed at [-110,10,0]: its pin center [20,10,0] maps to frame hole [-90,20,0], axis +X, with 0-LDU center/axis residual and nominal 20-LDU insertion. The second 30000 is at [19,10,-30], rotated to send its local +X pin to +Z; pin anchor [19,20,-10] matches the rail outer-face hole axis at [19,20,0] with 10-LDU reference offset along the axis, and 18.5/20-LDU nominal wall insertion. Its body is tangent to the rail exterior with no volume overlap. Root transform remains unverified."},{"pages":"18","steps":[17],"evidence":"Printed p.18 step17 shows a 64179 frame with four 2780 pins.","placement":"Nested in hogwarts-step14.ldr at position [79,80,0], matrix [0,0,1,-1,0,0,0,-1,0]. Its four side pins compose to [19,30,0], [59,30,0], [99,30,0], [139,30,0] with axes -Y; all align with the local 32278 rail row at x=19,59,99,139, y=20 and enter the adjoining 20-LDU layers. The combined step14–17 assembly remains root-unplaced."},{"pages":"18","steps":[18],"evidence":"Printed p.18 step18 callout shows one 90-degree gray L-shaped Technic beam and two pins. 32140 matches the visible 90-degree shape and candidate hole count, but no element number is printed.","placement":"Tentative local submodel hogwarts-step18.ldr: 32140 with 2780 pins in candidate holes (0,0,20) and (20,0,60). Axes/centers match the candidate DAT; part identity and selected holes remain uncertain. Not root reachable."},{"pages":"14","steps":[9],"evidence":"Booklet 22 printed p.14 step9 callout and result image. Official DAT headers confirm brown 2465 Brick 1 x 16 and gray 4282 Plate 2 x 16; p.14 image shows perpendicular long edges at the perimeter.","placement":"Partial local hogwarts-step9.ldr, tentative L arrangement sharing the visible corner datum. The pieces are individually placed, but no inter-part clutch or root attachment is claimed; overall transform to the existing foundation remains unresolved."},{"pages":"15","steps":[10],"evidence":"Booklet 22 printed p.15 step10 shows one tan and one gray mirrored tapered Technic panel. Official assets 67142 and 68196 headers identify the left/right Technic Panel 5x13 Curved #50/#51 Tapered shapes, matching the visible taper and pinhole pattern.","placement":"Partial local `hogwarts-step10.ldr`: 67142 and 68196 are aligned in one panel plane with a provisional 236-LDU seam interval and their lower bounds at local y=0. The image supports a paired panel module; exact lower support contacts and transform onto the foundation remain unverified."},{"pages":"15","steps":[11],"evidence":"Printed p.15 step11 callout and result show one gray 2x3 brick, two dark-green 2x1 slope bricks, and one cyan 1x2 brick. The silhouettes match official 3002, 3040b, and 3004 DATs.","placement":"Partial local `hogwarts-step11.ldr`: the four parts form a candidate contiguous stud-grid row at z centers 0,40,60,90. Brick/slope body footprints touch at the selected 20-LDU seams; the 3004 is centered on the shared row. Exact orientation/support contacts and transform onto steps1–10 remain provisional."},{"pages":"16","steps":[12],"evidence":"Printed p.16 step12 callout shows one gray small side-connector block and one tan three-hole tapered support. Candidate gray shapes 30000, 32064a, 3700, and 85943 have distinct footprint/connector mismatches; tan support has no unique matching registered shape.","placement":"Held pending unique part geometry and a visible matching connection. No placeholder or guessed shape is placed."},{"pages":"16","steps":[13],"evidence":"Printed p.16 step13 callout identifies one gray 1x3 plate, two tan 2x2 corner plates, one gray connector block, two gray 2x8 plates, and one gray 1x6 plate; shape candidates are 3623, 2420, 3034, and 3666 respectively.","placement":"No placement recorded yet. The final perspective shows the plate layer but hides the exact stud rows and transformations relative to the existing frame; 1x3/2x8/1x6 plate coordinates and connector identity remain to be resolved."}],"instances":[{"id":"part-0001","group":"frame","part":"3702.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":14,"position":[10,0,0],"matrix":[0,0,1,0,1,0,-1,0,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.10 step1; yellow studded Technic Brick 1x8 with seven side holes. Rotated so the seven-hole axis follows world Z; four 2780 pin centerlines are provisionally assigned to alternate holes z=-60,-20,20,60. Exact frame joint is pending multi-contact confirmation."},{"id":"part-0002","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[10,10,-60],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official booklet 3 PDF p.10 step1 pin. The 3702 DAT side-hole axes transform to world +X and alternate hole center is (10,10,-60); the 2780 local +X axis is world +X. Pin is located on the selected hole axis; nominal engagement depth is not marked verified until its insertion span and adjoining frame layer are resolved."},{"id":"part-0003","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[10,10,-20],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official booklet 3 PDF p.10 step1 pin. The 3702 DAT side-hole axes transform to world +X and alternate hole center is (10,10,-20); the 2780 local +X axis is world +X. Pin is located on the selected hole axis; nominal engagement depth is not marked verified until its insertion span and adjoining frame layer are resolved."},{"id":"part-0004","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[10,10,20],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official booklet 3 PDF p.10 step1 pin. The 3702 DAT side-hole axes transform to world +X and alternate hole center is (10,10,20); the 2780 local +X axis is world +X. Pin is located on the selected hole axis; nominal engagement depth is not marked verified until its insertion span and adjoining frame layer are resolved."},{"id":"part-0005","group":"frame","part":"2780.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":0,"position":[10,10,60],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official booklet 3 PDF p.10 step1 pin. The 3702 DAT side-hole axes transform to world +X and alternate hole center is (10,10,60); the 2780 local +X axis is world +X. Pin is located on the selected hole axis; nominal engagement depth is not marked verified until its insertion span and adjoining frame layer are resolved."},{"id":"part-0006","group":"frame","part":"3703.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[160,0,0],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.10 step2; dark bluish gray studded Technic Brick 1x16 with fifteen side holes. The type replaces the studless 32278 liftarm. Root position follows the visible extension from the 32531 frame and remains provisional pending exact pin-hole registration."},{"id":"part-0007","group":"frame","part":"6232.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,10,-50],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.11 step3; one dark bluish gray 2x2 brick with integral side pin and axlehole. Callout and inventory support type; retained connector location is provisional until its pin center is solved against the frame DAT."},{"id":"part-0008","group":"frame","part":"2458.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,10,-10],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.11 step3; one dark bluish gray 1x2 brick with integral side pin. Replaces the false 3700 female-hole candidate. Location/orientation remains provisional pending exact connector datum."},{"id":"part-0009","group":"frame","part":"6232.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,10,30],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.11 step4; one of three additional dark bluish gray 2x2 bricks with integral side pin and axlehole. Type and count are supported by callout and inventory; location is provisional."},{"id":"part-0010","group":"frame","part":"6232.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,10,70],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.11 step4; one of three additional dark bluish gray 2x2 bricks with integral side pin and axlehole. Type and count are supported by callout and inventory; location is provisional."},{"id":"part-0011","group":"frame","part":"6232.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,10,-90],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,0,1,0,-1,0],"catalog_mapping_status":"official_shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Official 71043 booklet 3 PDF p.11 step4; one of three additional dark bluish gray 2x2 bricks with integral side pin and axlehole. Type and count are supported by callout and inventory; location is provisional."},{"id":"part-0012","group":"frame","part":"32278.dat","gobricks_id":"","sku":"","color":72,"position":[0,48,70],"matrix":[1,0,0,0,1,0,0,0,1],"catalog_mapping_status":"shape_verified_sale_unmapped","placement_note":"Booklet 22 p.11 step5 second 32278.dat, provisionally below the 64179 long side aligned with its x=40 through-hole row (global x=0). Its body is y=38..58;